@page
@model BioModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Biography";
}

<div class="bio-page coffebackground">

    <div class="page-layout">

        <!-- MAIN TEXT -->
        <div class="page-content">

            <div class="page-intro">
                <h1>Biography</h1>
            </div>

            <div class="music page-section">

                <!-- BIOGRAPHY -->
                <section class="subsetion">
                    <p>
                        Born in 1978 in Brovary, Kyiv region.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Education</h2>

                    <p>
                        In 1996, graduated from the Lysenko Kyiv Special Music School
                        as a pianist.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        In 2000, graduated from the National Music Academy of Ukraine
                        (then named after Tchaikovsky) with degrees in piano
                        (class of Prof. V. O. Kozlov) and composition
                        (class of Prof. I. F. Karabyts).
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        In 2003, completed postgraduate internship at the National
                        Music Academy of Ukraine.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Participated in the master classes “Техника на компонирање”
                        (North Macedonia, 1999) and “Avantgarde Schwaz”
                        (Austria, 2000). Gaude Polonia scholarship programme (2004).
                    </p>
                </section>


                <section class="subsetion">
                    <h2>Competitions</h2>

                    <p>
                        Diploma recipient at the Rachmaninoff Young Pianists Competition
                        (Tambov, 1996).
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Diploma recipient at the Horowitz Competition (1997).
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Diploma recipient at the Marian and Ivanna Kots Competition
                        for Composers (Kyiv, 1994).
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Prize at the international competition “Creation of a Chamber
                        Opera on a Biblical Theme” (St. Petersburg, 2003).
                    </p>
                </section>


                <section class="subsetion">
                    <h2>Employment</h2>

                    <p>
                        Since 2001, I have worked at the Kyiv National University
                        of Culture and Arts as an accompanist, and since 2021
                        as a lecturer in piano, harmony, music informatics,
                        modern music information technologies, modern arranging
                        technologies (sample engineering), contemporary music,
                        and music project management.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        From 2008 to 2012, I taught at the Academy of Managerial
                        Personnel of Culture and Arts, teaching music informatics
                        and modern music information technologies.
                    </p>
                </section>


                <section class="subsetion">
                    <h2>Public Activity</h2>

                    <p>
                        Since 2006, contributor to the Ukrainian Wikipedia.<br>
                        In 2009, became one of the founders and the first Chairman
                        of the Board of Wikimedia Ukraine.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        In 2012, was the curator of the first “Wiki Loves Monuments”
                        competition in Ukraine.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        In 2015, served as Deputy Head of the Commission on Culture,
                        Art and Sectoral Education at the Ministry of Culture of Ukraine.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        In 2012, launched the project “World Classics in Ukrainian”,
                        aimed at reviving the tradition of performing vocal works
                        by composers of various national schools in Ukrainian translations.
                        The project included a series of vocal concerts and two vocal
                        competitions, “World Classics in Ukrainian” (2017, 2019).
                    </p>
                </section>

            </div>
        </div>


